  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Teyin may be a target of Tankyrase-2 through multiple pathways involving thioredoxin, 5-hydroxy-2-methylchromone-7-O-rutinoside, and isotorachrysone-6-O-alpha-D-ribofuranoside. These compounds are all identified as targets of Tankyrase-2, indicating a potential regulatory relationship where Tankyrase-2 influences the activity of these molecules. The scores for these relationships are consistent, with a final score of 0.5633 for one pathway and 0.5516 for the other two, suggesting a moderate level of confidence in the association. The overlapping targets, particularly thioredoxin, highlight a possible mechanism where Tankyrase-2 modulates the activity of thioredoxin, which in turn may affect cellular processes. The evidence supports a functional link between Teyin and Tankyrase-2, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
